# Pinned SHA-256 of the official Node.js archives bundled as runtime/ by
# scripts/package.mjs. Same format as https://nodejs.org/dist/v<ver>/SHASUMS256.txt.
# After bumping .node-version, replace the hash lines below with the output of:
#   v=$(sed 's/^v//' .node-version); curl -fsSL https://nodejs.org/dist/v$v/SHASUMS256.txt \
#     | grep -E "node-v$v-((darwin|linux)-(x64|arm64)\.tar\.gz|win-(x64|arm64)\.zip)$"
# For a stronger trust chain than TLS, also fetch SHASUMS256.txt.sig and check it
# with `gpg --verify` against the Node.js release keys (github.com/nodejs/node#release-keys).
